{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/178270-technocracy-as-inspiration","id":178270,"title":"Technocracy as inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-23T15:07:43-07:00","id":178270,"title":"Technocracy as inspiration","content":"How well could the Technocracy translate over as inspiration for a Demon Agency? I kind of think it could work...you have a group of agents, defending humanity in a broad sense, giving human pawns and servants &quot;hypertechnology&quot; gadgets, able to guide the development of humanity here and there...<br /> I dunno, maybe I'm just seeing too many parallels because I just fininshed a read of both Demon and Guide to the Technocracy, back to back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T15:11:41-07:00","id":178289,"title":"","content":"I would make them as a group of mortals serving thr God-Machine. One of the Hunter books (Witch Finders) has a group called Division Six that deals with 'reality deviants,' while another (Mortal Remains) covers two other anti-Demon groups. Stigmatics with Gadgets is probably the best way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T15:29:24-07:00","id":178304,"title":"","content":"In a thread from a while back we worked out the Technocracy as the product of the God-Machine, in a very limited way, being able to hack Awakenings and provide visions of the Utopias rather than the Realms. Either that or a stigmatic conspiracy make a lot of sense-and actually I like the Stigmatic conspiracy better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T00:46:14-07:00","id":181755,"title":"","content":"Well for one thing the easiest translation is the technocracy as a god-machine cult filled with stigmatics and generous helpings of infrastructure for all those gadgets. <br /> <br /> As a more demon friendly organization? Make them a conspiracy of those machinists or whatever they're called in the GMC. Stigmatics, demonblooded, and just plain muggles with unseen senses-god machine who have stolen and hacked enough infrastructure that they've become a third force in the angel-demon war. While not necessarily pro-demon, I imagine many demons would be willing to let some humans wreck the go-machine's plans by jacking its stuff. <br /> <br /> Perhaps demons who join the organization could be called kleptomaniacs, since I get the impression stealing from the god-machine isn't exactly considered sane in the demon community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T13:42:59-07:00","id":182189,"title":"","content":"As antagonists: a God-Machine cult of mortals and stigmatics that answers to either a Messenger Angel or some little cog of the Machine as 'Control.' They're empowered by a smattering of Gadgets and some demon-blooded that come from unknown and unpleasant sources.<br /> <br /> As allies: an Agency that consists largely of mortals and stigmatics with a small council of Inquisitors and Integrators. They don't just seek to destroy the God-Machine or escape its notice; they want to <i>become</i> a God-Machine of their own, suborning as much Infrastructure as they can in order to steer humanity towards a better future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T14:25:00-07:00","id":182229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/178270-technocracy-as-inspiration?p=182189#post182189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As antagonists: a God-Machine cult of mortals and stigmatics that answers to either a Messenger Angel or some little cog of the Machine as 'Control.' They're empowered by a smattering of Gadgets and some demon-blooded that come from unknown and unpleasant sources.<br /> As allies: an Agency that consists largely of mortals and stigmatics with a small council of Inquisitors and Integrators. They don't just seek to destroy the God-Machine or escape its notice; they want to <i>become</i> a God-Machine of their own, suborning as much Infrastructure as they can in order to steer humanity towards a better future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like your second idea. Not that I didn't like the other ones, but your second one is closer to what I was seeing. I can imagine that there would still be some Demons at the Front Lines, but supported mostly by regular humans and stigmatics, backed up by mass produced Gadgets (is that even possible)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:50:50-07:00","id":182372,"title":"","content":"...I just realized my Agency is almost identical to Utopia Now, from Mortal Remains. Whoops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T17:37:30-07:00","id":182392,"title":"","content":"Looks like I have another book to add to the wishlist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T16:33:34-07:00","id":183338,"title":"","content":"<b>Agency: The Technocratic Union</b><br /> <br /> There exists a great Machine that controls reality from behind the scenes. This Machine is not the kindly divine creator so many pray to, but a callous demiurge that regards humanity as little more than playthings. It hides behind an infinite number of masks, burying alien programs in the metaphysical fabric of the city. The Machine has an understanding of physics that enables it to do things most think impossible - you know the old line about 'sufficiently advanced technology' and all that, right? Destroying the Machine isn't possible; it's too deeply embedded in the infrastructure that keeps the world running. The thing is, it isn't impervious to assault. Its tools can be stolen. Its understanding can be gained. The Machine can be <i>used</i>, if one knows where to push. <br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union largely consists of Stigmatic mortals, led by a handful of Integrators and Inquisitors who have banded together.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mission:</b> Use the Machine for good. Guide humanity towards prosperity (and an eventually technological Singularity). Those who comprise the Technocratic Union know the God-Machine exists, and hopes to use the assets it has to build a better future. No small number of transhumanists occupy the Technocratic Union's membership, hoping to use Gadgets to become something <i>better</i> than what they were born as. The council of Unchained that lead the Technocratic Union hope to replace the 'brain' of the God-Machine, guiding it towards their new purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>Resources</b>: Not much, as of yet. The Unchained in charge spend most of their time churning out Gadgets for their agents to use, and have a few boltholes and bits of suborned Infrastructure across [whatever city your chronicle is set in].<br /> <br /> <b>Who's In Charge: </b>The council of Demons who lead the Technocratic Union are referred to as Control by the stigmatics who make up the bulk of membership. They're Integrators and Inquisitors (or more appropriately, Integrator-Inquisitors) with the mother of all goals.<br /> <br /> <b>What's Falling Apart: </b>Plausibility. One ring of demons and a little more than two dozen Stigmatics don't stand much chance of taking down a supernatural entity that spans the globe. They have little to no cash flow and no ready way of replacing those killed by Angels. Control struggles to supply enough Gadgets to give mortal agents a chance in the field. Recruitment is little more than stumbling across Stigmatics in the field and hoping they hop aboard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}